Description: offline push-to-talk dictation for the desktop
 Myna captures the microphone while a shortcut is active, sends the audio to
 a local speech-to-text engine over a Unix socket, and types the transcript
 into the focused application through IBus. Nothing leaves the machine.
 .
 This package ships the dictation daemon (myna-desktop, run as the
 myna.service user unit), the HUD renderer (myna-hud), the myna-testbed
 development tool, and the GSettings schema. It needs an inference engine
 such as myna-whisper. Built natively for Debian, without snapd.
